          "finalAnswer": "Based on the provided observations:\n\n**File and Function**\nThe rate limiting is enforced in `src/middleware/throttle.ts` by the exported `throttle(apiKey, now)` function. It tracks request timestamps per API key using an in-memory `Map<string, number[]>`.\n\n**Limit and Time Window**\nThe service uses a sliding window approach with these exact constants:\n- **Time Window:** `WINDOW_MS = 60_000` (60 seconds)\n- **Request Limit:** `MAX_REQUESTS = 30`\nEach call to `throttle` filters the stored timestamps, keeping only those within the last 60 seconds. If the filtered count reaches 30, the request is blocked.\n\n**Client Response on Exceeding the Limit**\nWhen the limit is exceeded, the function returns a response object containing:\n- `status`: `429`\n- `body`: `{ \"error\": \"too many requests\", \"retryAfter\": <calculated integer> }`\nThe `retryAfter` value is dynamically computed as the number of seconds until the oldest request in the current window expires, telling the client exactly how long to wait before retrying.",
